# Commits & pushing

## Never commit unless explicitly asked

- Do not create a commit unless the user explicitly says "commit", "make a commit", or similar.
- Do not push unless the user explicitly says "push".
- Never run `git commit --amend` or force operations without explicit request. Never use `push --force` on `main`.

## Before committing

Always, in this order:

```bash
yarn typecheck
yarn lint
yarn test
yarn build        # must succeed (TypeScript + vite build together)
```

`yarn verify` runs all four in sequence. If any step fails, stop and surface the failure to the user — do not "fix" by adding `// @ts-expect-error`, disabling ESLint rules inline, or skipping tests.

## Commit message format (Conventional Commits)

`<type>(<optional-scope>): <short summary in imperative mood>`

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `perf`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`, `style`.

Examples:

```
feat(products): add carrara marble napkin variants
fix(cart): correct total when quantity changes during checkout
chore(deps): bump @vercel/blob to 2.3.3
test(home): cover parallax hero image with e2e smoke test
```

- No emojis in commit messages.
- Subject line under 72 chars, no trailing period.
- If the change is non‑trivial, add a blank line and a body that explains *why*.

## Files never to stage

- `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`
- Anything containing `BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN` or other secrets
- `dist/`, `coverage/`, `playwright-report/`, `test-results/`, `.vercel/`

If `git status` shows any of these as staged, abort and ask.

## Pushing

- Default remote is the branch's tracked upstream. If the branch has no upstream, use `git push -u origin HEAD`.
- Never push directly to `main` — open a PR. If the user asks to push to `main`, confirm first.
- After pushing a PR, a Vercel preview deployment is created automatically; include the preview URL in the PR description when relevant.
